 Cached JPEG data may occupy at most 12 GiB. Before admitting a completed sheet, evict enough existing sheets to remain within that bound. Temporary render output is kept separately and removed on completion or failure. Eviction never deletes source footage or changes job-ticket semantics.
 
-The eviction policy is still open. Candidates are LRU, frequency-based eviction with aging, and 2Q. LRU has little bookkeeping and follows recent work quickly but is vulnerable to sequential scans. Aged frequency counts protect repeatedly popular clips but add counter maintenance and can lag a project switch. 2Q separates first-use entries from reused entries, resisting scans at the cost of extra queues and a queue-size parameter. None changes the external interface, queue concurrency, or disk budget.
+## Replacement Policy (2Q)
+
+The cache uses 2Q replacement so that sheets seen once during a long screening do not displace sheets editors return to for comparison. All state described here is private to the preview worker.
+
+- **First-use queue**: FIFO of cached sheets that have not yet shown reuse. A sheet enters here on admission, unless its key is in the ghost list.
+- **Reused queue**: LRU of cached sheets that have shown reuse.
+- **Ghost list**: FIFO of preview keys (no JPEG data) recently evicted from the first-use queue. A sheet whose key is found here when it is admitted goes directly to the reused queue.
+- **Size split**: the first-use queue is bounded to a configured fraction of the 12 GiB budget, measured in bytes of JPEG data. The reused queue may use the remainder. The fraction is a worker configuration value.
+
+Eviction runs before admission (see Private Cache). While the first-use queue exceeds its fraction, evict from its head and record the key in the ghost list; otherwise evict from the least recently used end of the reused queue. A cache hit on a reused-queue sheet moves it to the most recently used end. Pending-response polling is not a cache hit and does not affect queue position.
+
+The external interface, render queue concurrency, and 12 GiB budget are independent of this policy.
+
+## Decisions & Alternatives
+
+| Decision | Chosen | Alternatives Considered | Rationale |
+|----------|--------|------------------------|-----------|
+| Replacement policy | 2Q | LRU; frequency-based eviction with aging | Editors alternate long sequential screenings with repeated comparisons of a small set. LRU lets a screening scan evict comparison sheets. Aged frequency counts retain popular clips but add counter maintenance and can keep a past project's favorites too long. 2Q protects reused sheets from one-use scans at the cost of two queues, a ghost list, and a size-split parameter. |
+| Size split unit | Bytes of cached JPEG data | Entry count | The disk bound is in bytes. |
+
